    optionRight: Triangle
    isLeftCorrect: 0
  - questionText: How many days did it take to build the new red-brick factory
    optionLeft: 'About 100 days '
    optionRight: 'About 330 days '
    isLeftCorrect: 0
  - questionText: Were the factory mine cars used to transport anything other than
      beer
    optionLeft: Charcoal
    optionRight: Ice
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: What was the item that began to be used in place of cork stoppers
      around Meiji 39 and was standardized in Taisho 6
    optionLeft: 'Crown Cap '
    optionRight: 'Screw-on Lid '
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: 'Which American fighter left traces of machine-gun fire in Showa
      20 '
    optionLeft: 'North American P-51 '
    optionRight: 'Zero Fighter '
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: What kind of clothes did the people who worked at the factory back
      then wear
    optionLeft: 'Wearing work overalls '
    optionRight: 'Wearing a happi coat '
    isLeftCorrect: 0
  - questionText: 'Whose house was located at the southwest corner of the current
      Handa Red Brick Building '
    optionLeft: 'German engineer '
    optionRight: 'American Engineer '
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: 'Which of these didn''t actually exist around the Red Brick Building
      back then '
    optionLeft: 'Bottling plants and coal storage yards '
    optionRight: 'Airport Runway '
    isLeftCorrect: 0
  - questionText: How large was the site area of the Handa Plant
    optionLeft: '10,000 tsubo '
    optionRight: '100 tsubo '
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: 'At what temperature were the red bricks fired to oxidize them '
    optionLeft: "500\u2103 "
    optionRight: "1100\u2103 "
    isLeftCorrect: 0
  - questionText: How were red bricks molded
    optionLeft: 'Embossing Machine Molding '
    optionRight: 'Hand-Molding by Hand '
    isLeftCorrect: 0
  - questionText: What's inside the red brick
    optionLeft: 'Stamped Mark '
    optionRight: 'Sign '
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: Which is the correct way to lay red bricks in Handa
    optionLeft: 'Shipped from the UK '
    optionRight: 'French-style stacking '
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: 'If you make bricks using a wooden form, how will the finished
      product compare to the form '
    optionLeft: 'It will grow by about 20 percent '
    optionRight: 'Shrinks by about 20 percent '
    isLeftCorrect: 0
  - questionText: What is the name of the architectural style in which the spaces
      between wooden posts and beams are filled with bricks
    optionLeft: 'Half-Timber '
    optionRight: 'Log Cabin '
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: What was embedded in the walls as insulation for beer aging
    optionLeft: Cork
    optionRight: Styrofoam
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: Which material was spread in the attic for insulation
    optionLeft: Sawdust and rice husks
    optionRight: Gravel and newspapers
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: What is the structure in the ceiling of the first floor that is
      fire-resistant and has heat insulation effects
    optionLeft: Great Fire-resistant Floor (Taikasho)
    optionRight: Grand Staircase
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: What was carried on the mine carts on the way back after transporting
      beer
    optionLeft: Raw materials (barley and hops)
    optionRight: Food and daily necessities
    isLeftCorrect: 0
  - questionText: Approximately how many liters of beer were in one barrel in the
      beer cellar
    optionLeft: Approx. 600 liters
    optionRight: Approx. 6,000 liters
    isLeftCorrect: 0
  - questionText: What clever feature did the walls of the beer cellar have to pack
      the barrels closely together
    optionLeft: The walls are curved
    optionRight: ' The walls are entirely glassed'
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: What was the straw matting (Komo) used to wrap the beer made of
    optionLeft: Barley
    optionRight: Vinyl / Plastic
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: Where overseas was Kabuto Beer exported to
    optionLeft: Germany
    optionRight: Brazil
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: At which global event did Kabuto Beer win the Gold Medal
    optionLeft: Paris Exposition Universelle
    optionRight: Great London Exposition
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: Which floor of the Red Brick Building was mainly used as the aging
      storage room
    optionLeft: 1st floor
    optionRight: 2nd floor
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: What structure did the first floor have to effectively utilize
      it for beer storage
    optionLeft: Semi-underground structure
    optionRight: On-water structure
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: At what temperature did young beer need to be stored for 90 days
    optionLeft: "0\u2103"
    optionRight: "20\u2103"
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: 'Origin of the name Kabuto Beer 1: Which word means drinking alcohol
      energetically/heartily'
    optionLeft: Kaburu
    optionRight: Haneru
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: 'Origin of the name Kabuto Beer 2: Which proverb was the base for
      the name'
    optionLeft: 'Don''t rest on your laurels (literally: Tighten your helmet strap
      after winning)'
    optionRight: 'Surrender (literally: Take off your helmet)'
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: Which of the following was NOT something Kabuto Beer signage was
      used on
    optionLeft: Sumo ceremonial aprons (kesho-mawashi) and matchboxes
    optionRight: Space rocket hulls
    isLeftCorrect: 0
  - questionText: At which station did a large Kabuto Beer advertising tower stand
    optionLeft: Nagoya Station
    optionRight: Tokyo Station
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: What was the feature of the envelopes used for Kabuto Beer's business
      operations
    optionLeft: Window envelopes
    optionRight: Double-layered envelopes
    isLeftCorrect: 0
  - questionText: Which domestic event did Kabuto Beer exhibit at and gain popularity
    optionLeft: National Industrial Exhibition
    optionRight: National Delicious Food Fair
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: What was the longest rebar inserted into the brick walls during
      seismic reinforcement work
    optionLeft: 21 meters
    optionRight: 3 meters
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: How long does it take to age Kabuto Beer
    optionLeft: 3 weeks
    optionRight: 3 months
    isLeftCorrect: 0
  - questionText: Which of the following is NOT a correct role of hops
    optionLeft: Adding bitterness and aroma, and suppressing bacterial growth
    optionRight: Making the beer sweet and coloring it red
    isLeftCorrect: 0
  - questionText: What effect does the property of the red brick itself give to the
      building
    optionLeft: Thermal insulation effect to protect from outside heat
    optionRight: Cooling effect to cool the room
    isLeftCorrect: 1
  - questionText: Approximately how many bricks were used in total for the entire
      Red Brick Building
    optionLeft: Approx. 200,000
    optionRight: Approx. 2,000
    isLeftCorrect: 1
